{ "Identifier":       { "ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "MMC-MAT-V2.5-I01", "AIMName": "MMC-MAT-V2.5" },

  "APIProfile":       "Basic",
  "Description":      "Multimodal Anonymous Translation: the HCI middleware Module for anonymous speech-to-speech translation with a speaking avatar (no identity - no ID Reconciliation). A trusted composite exposing the north HCI API to a User Agent application. It recognises the human's speech (Automatic Speech Recognition), translates the recognised text into the language named by the Language Selector (Text-to-Text Translation), speaks the translation (Text-To-Speech, in the target-language voice) and produces the Machine Face Descriptors that lip-sync the translated speech (Generative Face Description). The input language rides on the input Speech Qualifier; the target language is named by the Language Selector and carried onward by the translated text's Qualifier, so Text-To-Speech selects the target voice. The person speaks in one language; the avatar speaks the translation in another, lip-synced. Reuses the ASR/TTT/TTS pipeline.",

